From: Tsuyoshi Horo <horo@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:39:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/22] [M156] [blink] Clear background streamer on script
 revalidation

Original change's description:
> [blink] Clear background streamer on script revalidation
>
> When a ScriptResource that previously used
> BackgroundResourceScriptStreamer is revalidated,
> SetRevalidatingRequest() cleared streamer_ and cache_consumer_, but did
> not clear background_streamer_.
>
> If the revalidation response subsequently failed (non-304),
> DestroyDecodedDataForFailedRevalidation() cleared source_text_, but
> ResponseReceived() immediately re-installed the stale decoded text from
> the surviving background_streamer_. This caused the resource to execute
> the previous response's text while creating a
> ScriptCachedMetadataHandler bound to the new response, leading to a
> mismatched code cache in V8.
>
> This CL resolves the issue by:
> 1. Clearing background_streamer_ in SetRevalidatingRequest(), matching
>    the existing handling of streamer_ and cache_consumer_.
> 2. Adding a DCHECK(!background_streamer_) in
>    DestroyDecodedDataForFailedRevalidation().
> 3. Adding unit tests for both successful (304) and failed (200)
>    revalidations with background streaming.
>
